-- from 16 runs to 11 slots --

The 16 rows above collapse to 13 distinct (task, configuration, rep) SLOTS. Three
tasks contributed two attempts at the same slot:

  w3 P0 rep1   screening-batch1 (1800s flat bound) + screening-batch1-makeup (7200s, the task's own pinned budget)
  w3 P1 rep1   screening-batch1 (1800s flat bound) + screening-batch1-makeup (7200s, the task's own pinned budget)
  w6 C2 rep2   screening-batch1 (0-byte diff, VOID on the review_diff delivery defect) + screening-batch1-makeup-w6 (1200s claude_timeout)

The two W3 slots are NOT bought again. They were re-bought once already, at the
budget their own task pins, and cut off again. "Does not complete within 2h at
this task's pinned budget" is a RESULT, not a hole — a budget-exhaustion finding
carried in the limitation ledger, citing both attempts. Buying a third would be
buying the same answer.

The W6 slot IS bought. Its batch-1 attempt is void on a delivery defect (no
review_diff reached the agent), so it is not a second observation of anything:
this pass is only its second attempt under a working instrument, and one
truncation is a loss, not a measurement. It lands in this dataset rather than in
screening-batch1-makeup-w6 because that dataset already holds a run for the cell
and its resume index would count the slot settled and skip it.

  13 slots - 2 budget-exhaustion findings = 11 runs planned.

Every slot is re-bought under ITS OWN task's pinned agent_timeout_s, not the flat
1800s bound that censored it; the driver refuses any task whose task.yaml does not
carry the expected budget. A truncated original and its replacement are never
pooled: they are observations under different instrument settings.
